# CODEOWNERS — review routing for money/schema/security-sensitive paths.
#
# Real-org-membership check (2026-08-28, docs/audit/2026-08-27-cicd-gates-
# guardrails-audit.md Section 3 / ACTION_ITEMS.md E8): this repo currently
# has exactly 2 collaborators and 0 GitHub teams (confirmed via the GitHub
# API, not assumed) --
#   @srikumarimuddana-lab  -- admin (the account/org owner)
#   @ittalenthireca-sketch -- write (opens/authors PRs; per this repo's own
#                              observed history, effectively the PR-author
#                              identity on most PRs)
#
# Both accounts are listed below (OR semantics -- either one's approval
# satisfies the rule). IMPORTANT caveat: GitHub never counts a PR's own
# author as a valid approver for required-review/CODEOWNERS purposes, even
# when that author is a listed code owner. Since @ittalenthireca-sketch
# authors most PRs in this repo, listing it here only adds real coverage
# on PRs it does NOT author (e.g. one @srikumarimuddana-lab opens, or a
# future third collaborator) -- it does not let @ittalenthireca-sketch
# self-approve its own PRs. On PRs @ittalenthireca-sketch opens,
# @srikumarimuddana-lab's approval remains the only one that counts.
#
# The domain-team routing this file used to name (`@spinr-org/TBD-payments-
# reviewers` etc.) was never real -- there is no `spinr-org` GitHub
# organization with those teams, so GitHub could never resolve those
# handles and "Require review from Code Owners" could never have enforced
# anything even if branch protection enabled it. Replaced below with the
# real accounts this repo actually has. The domain structure is kept (not
# collapsed to a single `*` rule) because it's real, useful documentation
# of which paths are money/schema/security/dispatch/safety-sensitive --
# matching the same domain boundaries `.github/labeler.yml` and
# `ci-guardrails.yml`'s `risk-label`/`change-impact-log-gate` jobs already
# use -- and because it's a one-line-per-domain edit to point at a real
# team the moment one exists, rather than a redesign.
#
# Rules are evaluated bottom-up: the last matching pattern wins, so more
# specific paths are listed after more general ones.
#
# TO EXTEND once real per-domain reviewers/teams exist: replace the
# relevant domain's owners below with `@spinr-org/<real-team-slug>` (a team
# GitHub can actually resolve), then enable "Require review from Code
# Owners" in Settings -> Branches -> main (see docs/audit/2026-08-27-cicd-
# gates-guardrails-audit.md Section 1 for the rest of that branch-
# protection checklist).

